  "output": "Now I have a full picture of the codebase. This is the \"Canon\" Next.js console app — no test framework is installed at all and there are zero test files. Here's the coverage analysis.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Critical gap: zero test infrastructure.** No Jest/Vitest, no test files, no `test` script in `package.json`. Every function below is untested by definition. Recommend adding **Vitest** (fast, native ESM/TS, works well with Next.js 16 + React 19) plus `@testing-library/react` for components.\n\n```bash\nnpm i -D vitest @vitejs/plugin-react @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom jsdom\n```\n\n---\n\n## 1. `lib/reviewer-label.ts` — `reviewerLabel()`\n\nPure function, highest-value target (drives both UI identity and audit-log actor). Untested precedence chain: username → email → fallback.\n\n```ts\n// lib/reviewer-label.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { reviewerLabel } from \"./reviewer-label\";\n\ndescribe(\"reviewerLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"prefers username over email and fallback\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"j.rao\", primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"uid_1\")).toBe(\"j.rao\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to email when username is null\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"uid_1\")).toBe(\"j@x.com\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to userId when both username and email are missing\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: null }, \"uid_1\")).toBe(\"uid_1\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to userId when user is null\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel(null, \"uid_1\")).toBe(\"uid_1\");\n  });\n\n  // edge case: empty-string username should NOT be treated as missing (?? vs ||)\n  it(\"treats empty-string username as present (not falsy-coerced)\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"\", primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"uid_1\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back when emailAddress is present but undefined\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: undefined, primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: undefined } }, \"uid_1\")).toBe(\"uid_1\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n*Gap flagged*: the `??` chain means an empty string `\"\"` username currently wins over a real email — worth confirming that's intended before locking it in a test.\n\n## 2. `lib/server/auth.ts` — `requireReviewer()` / `getReviewer()`\n\nNo coverage of the auth-disagreement failure path or the signed-out branch. Needs mocking `@clerk/nextjs/server` and `reviewerLabel`.\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/auth.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { auth, currentUser } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\nimport { requireReviewer, getReviewer } from \"./auth\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\", () => ({\n  auth: vi.fn(),\n  currentUser: vi.fn(),\n}));\n\ndescribe(\"requireReviewer\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => vi.clearAllMocks());\n\n  it(\"returns userId + label when authenticated\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"uid_1\" } as any);\n    vi.mocked(currentUser).mockResolvedValue({ username: \"j.rao\" } as any);\n\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"uid_1\", label: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is false\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false, userId: null } as any);\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow(/No authenticated reviewer/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is true but userId is missing (matcher/handler disagreement)\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: undefined } as any);\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow(/No authenticated reviewer/);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when signed out\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false } as any);\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"delegates to requireReviewer when signed in\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"uid_1\" } as any);\n    vi.mocked(currentUser).mockResolvedValue({ username: \"j.rao\" } as any);\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"uid_1\", label: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## 3. `types/rules.ts` — `ruleSpecificity()`\n\nUntested ordering logic that determines which survivorship rule wins — a correctness bug here silently changes which value survives a conflict.\n\n```ts\n// types/rules.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ruleSpecificity, survivorshipRuleSchema, createRulesetSchema } from \"./rules\";\n\nconst base = { id: \"r1\", strategy: \"escalate\" as const, description: \"d\" };\n\ndescribe(\"ruleSpecificity\", () => {\n  it(\"wildcard field + wildcard entityType = 0\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ ...base, field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" })).toBe(0);\n  });\n  it(\"exact field + wildcard entityType = 2\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ ...base, field: \"name\", entityType: \"*\" })).toBe(2);\n  });\n  it(\"wildcard field + exact entityType = 1\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ ...base, field: \"*\", entityType: \"account\" })).toBe(1);\n  });\n  it(\"exact field + exact entityType = 3 (most specific)\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ ...base, field: \"name\", entityType: \"account\" })).toBe(3);\n  });\n\n  it(\"sorting a set of rules by specificity descending yields first-match-wins order\", () => {\n    const rules = [\n      { ...base, id: \"wild\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" },\n      { ...base, id: \"specific\", field: \"name\", entityType: \"account\" },\n      { ...base, id: \"field-only\", field: \"name\", entityType: \"*\" },\n    ];\n    const sorted = [...rules].sort((a, b) => ruleSpecificity(b) - ruleSpecificity(a));\n    expect(sorted.map((r) => r.id)).toEqual([\"specific\", \"field-only\", \"wild\"]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"survivorshipRuleSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects prefer_source without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\", description: \"d\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts prefer_source with preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\",\n      preferredSourceId: \"src_1\", description: \"d\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts most_recent/most_complete/escalate without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    for (const strategy of [\"most_recent\", \"most_complete\", \"escalate\"] as const) {\n      expect(survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n        id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy, description: \"d\",\n      }).success).toBe(true);\n    }\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"createRulesetSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty rules array\", () => {\n    expect(createRulesetSchema.safeParse({ name: \"v1\", rules: [] }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## 4. `lib/server/sources.ts` — `listSources()` / `countSourcesBySide()`\n\nNo coverage of the CRM/warehouse/synthetic bucketing, and no test that `sourceSchema.parse` actually rejects a malformed DB row. Requires mocking `getDb()` and `connection()`.\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/sources.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { countSourcesBySide, listSources } from \"./sources\";\nimport { getDb } from \"@/lib/db\";\n\nvi.mock(\"next/server\", () => ({ connection: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined) }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/db\", () => ({ getDb: vi.fn() }));\n\nfunction mockRows(rows: unknown[]) {\n  vi.mocked(getDb).mockReturnValue({\n    select: () => ({ from: () => ({ orderBy: () => Promise.resolve(rows) }) }),\n  } as any);\n}\n\ndescribe(\"countSourcesBySide\", () => {\n  it(\"buckets salesforce/hubspot as crm, databricks/snowflake as warehouse, synthetic separately\", async () => {\n    mockRows([\n      row({ kind: \"salesforce\" }), row({ kind: \"hubspot\" }),\n      row({ kind: \"databricks\" }), row({ kind: \"snowflake\" }),\n      row({ kind: \"synthetic\" }),\n    ]);\n    await expect(countSourcesBySide()).resolves.toEqual({ crm: 2, warehouse: 2, synthetic: 1 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns all zeros when there are no sources\", async () => {\n    mockRows([]);\n    await expect(countSourcesBySide()).resolves.toEqual({ crm: 0, warehouse: 0, synthetic: 0 });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"listSources\", () => {\n  it(\"throws if a stored row fails sourceSchema validation (e.g. malformed config)\", async () => {\n    mockRows([{ id: \"not-a-uuid\", name: \"x\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: {}, createdAt: new Date() }]);\n    await expect(listSources()).rejects.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\nfunction row(overrides: Partial<Record<string, unknown>>) {\n  return {\n    id: \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n    name: \"Test\",\n    config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n    createdAt: new Date(),\n    ...overrides,\n  };\n}\n```\n\n## 5. `proxy.ts` — route protection matcher\n\nThe single most security-sensitive piece of logic in the app (auth gate for the entire console) has no test verifying which routes are public vs. protected.\n\n```ts\n// proxy.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { createRouteMatcher } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\n\n// Re-declare matcher inline (or export isPublicRoute from proxy.ts for direct testing)\nconst isPublicRoute = createRouteMatcher([\"/\", \"/sign-in(.*)\", \"/sign-up(.*)\"]);\n\nfunction req(path: string) {\n  return new Request(`https://example.com${path}`);\n}\n\ndescribe(\"isPublicRoute\", () => {\n  it.each([\"/\", \"/sign-in\", \"/sign-in/factor-one\", \"/sign-up\"])(\n    \"%s is public\",\n    (path) => expect(isPublicRoute(req(path))).toBe(true),\n  );\n\n  it.each([\"/sources\", \"/api/sources\", \"/get-started\", \"/sign-in-typo\"])(\n    \"%s requires auth\",\n    (path) => expect(isPublicRoute(req(path))).toBe(false),\n  );\n});\n```\n\n*Note*: `isPublicRoute` currently isn't exported from `proxy.ts` — exporting it (or extracting to `lib/route-matcher.ts`) is a prerequisite for direct testing rather than only integration-testing the composed middleware.\n\n## 6. `lib/cn.ts` — `cn()`\n\nTrivial but worth locking down since every styled component depends on Tailwind class dedup behavior.\n\n```ts\n// lib/cn.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { cn } from \"./cn\";\n\ndescribe(\"cn\", () => {\n  it(\"merges class strings\", () => expect(cn(\"a\", \"b\")).toBe(\"a b\"));\n  it(\"drops falsy values\", () => expect(cn(\"a\", false, null, undefined, \"b\")).toBe(\"a b\"));\n  it(\"lets tailwind-merge resolve conflicting utility classes\", () => {\n    expect(cn(\"px-2\", \"px-4\")).toBe(\"px-4\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## 7. Zod schemas (`types/*.ts`) — no round-trip/reject tests\n\nNone of the schemas that gate data entering the DB or leaving the API (`createSourceSchema`, `canonicalEntitySchema`, `conflictSchema`, `resolutionSchema`, `reviewActionSchema`, `runSchema`) have tests confirming they reject bad input. `reviewActionSchema`'s discriminated union is the highest-risk one — it's what enforces `reviewedBy` never comes from the client.\n\n```ts\n// types/resolution.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { reviewActionSchema } from \"./resolution\";\n\ndescribe(\"reviewActionSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts approve/reject with no extra fields\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"approve\" }).success).toBe(true);\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"reject\" }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"requires overrideValue for override, and rejects empty string\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\" }).success).toBe(false);\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\", overrideValue: \"\" }).success).toBe(false);\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\", overrideValue: \"x\" }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects a client-supplied reviewedBy field being relied upon (schema has no such field)\", () => {\n    const parsed = reviewActionSchema.parse({ action: \"approve\", reviewedBy: \"spoofed\" });\n    expect(parsed).not.toHaveProperty(\"reviewedBy\"); // stripped, not trusted\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects unknown action values\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"delete\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// types/source.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { createSourceSchema, sourceConfigSchema } from \"./source\";\n\ndescribe(\"createSourceSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty objects array in config\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [] }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects name over 80 chars\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({\n      name: \"x\".repeat(81), kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n    }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an unknown source kind\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({\n      name: \"x\", kind: \"bigquery\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] },\n    }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## 8. Component tests — none exist\n\n- `components/severity-mark.tsx`: no test that all 4 severities render both the glyph and the required word (this is an explicit accessibility/AGENTS.md constraint — \"never rendered without the word\").\n- `components/sources/source-table.tsx`: no test for empty `sources` array, or that `SOURCE_KIND_LABEL`/`SOURCE_KIND_SIDE` lookups don't throw for every enum value.\n\n```tsx\n// components/severity-mark.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SeverityMark } from \"./severity-mark\";\nimport { SEVERITY_LABEL, type Severity } from \"@/types/conflict\";\n\ndescribe(\"SeverityMark\", () => {\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4] as Severity[])(\"severity %d always renders its label word, not just the mark\", (s) => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={s} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(SEVERITY_LABEL[s])).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```tsx\n// components/sources/source-table.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SourceTable } from \"./source-table\";\n\ndescribe(\"SourceTable\", () => {\n  it(\"renders an empty tbody with no rows when sources is []\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[]} />);\n    expect(screen.queryAllByRole(\"row\")).toHaveLength(1); // header row only\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders name, kind label, side, and joined objects for a source\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[{\n      id: \"1\", name: \"Acme SFDC\", kind: \"salesforce\",\n      config: { objects: [\"Account\", \"Contact\"] }, createdAt: new Date(),\n    }]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Acme SFDC\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Salesforce\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"crm\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Account, Contact\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## 9. Integration gaps (no test surface at all today)\n\n- **No route handler tests** — `app/(console)/sources/page.tsx` presumably calls `listSources()`/auth; there's no test that a signed-out request to a protected route actually redirects (this is only enforced by `proxy.ts`, which itself is untested — see #5).\n- **No DB integration tests** — nothing exercises `lib/db/schema.ts` against a real/test Postgres instance (e.g. via `drizzle-kit` + a Docker Postgres or `pg-mem`) to confirm foreign keys (`runs.sourceAId → sources.id`, etc.) actually enforce referential integrity.\n- **No test for the \"ownership boundary\" comment in schema.ts** — e.g., there's no runtime check anywhere that web code never writes to `entities`/`matches`/`conflicts` (engine-owned tables). Worth at least a static/lint-level guard or an integration test that asserts no web-side Drizzle `insert`/`update` targets those tables.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended priority order\n1. Add Vitest + config (`vitest.config.ts` with `@` path alias resolution matching `tsconfig.json`).\n2. `reviewerLabel`, `ruleSpecificity`, zod schemas — pure, zero-mock, highest ROI.\n3. `proxy.ts` route matcher — security-critical, currently only implicitly trusted.\n4. `lib/server/auth.ts`, `lib/server/sources.ts` — need Clerk/DB mocks but guard the audit trail's integrity.\n5. Component smoke tests for `SeverityMark`/`SourceTable`.\n6. DB/integration tests once there's a CI Postgres available.\n",
